asr-000014
00:01:52.300 --> 00:02:03.000
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you very much, ComSec. So, uh, first of all, let me welcome our Honorable Ombudsman,

asr-000015
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:10.300
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: our very own was with us in the congress the house of representatives uh former secretary of justice

asr-000016
00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:14.540
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: now the Ombudsman, Boying. Welcome.

asr-000017
00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:21.500
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: i would also like to welcome everyone for this briefing of the office of the ombudsman

asr-000018
00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:28.780
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: headed by Ombudsman Remulla. The Office of the Ombudsman, one of the constitutional bodies

asr-000019
00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:40.460
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: established under the 1987 constitution has a recommended budget of 7.06 billion for fiscal year

asr-000020
00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:48.760
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: 2027. This represents an increase of approximately 10%.

asr-000021
00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:59.420
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: from its current fiscal year 2026 budget of 6.42 billion and accounts for

asr-000022
00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:11.020
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: about 0.15 percent of the 4.6-trillion national government budget. This proposed increase will

asr-000023
00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:13.260
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: provide additional resources

asr-000024
00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:15.660
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: to strengthen the Office's mandate

asr-000025
00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:23.600
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: and key programs, particularly its Anti-Corruption Investigation Program, the Anti-Corruption

asr-000026
00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:31.360
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Enforcement Program, the Ombudsman Public Assistance Program, and the Corruption Prevention

asr-000027
00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:32.760
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Program.

asr-000028
00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:40.720
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: The Office of the Ombudsman plays a vital role in upholding accountability—I repeat

asr-000029
00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:47.020
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: again—accountability and integrity in public service.

asr-000030
00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:54.040
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Through the investigation and case build-up, as well as the enforcement of administrative,

asr-000031
00:03:54.040 --> 00:04:03.620
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: civil and criminal liability, the Office contributes significantly to ensuring that they will

asr-000032
00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:10.700
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: effectively be able to—the government operates efficiently, responsibly, and effectively

asr-000033
00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:13.260
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: and in accordance with law.

asr-000034
00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:19.100
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Given this crucial mandate, the Office of the Ombudsman rightly looks to Congress, and

asr-000035
00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:25.120
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: particularly the House of Representatives, for the necessary budgetary support to enable

asr-000036
00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:34.600
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: it to effectively discharge its constitutional functions—not only for fiscal year 2027

asr-000037
00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:36.340
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: but also in the years ahead.

asr-000038
00:04:37.253 --> 00:04:41.455
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: At the same time, we recognize that every peso appropriated

asr-000042
00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:47.058
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: by Congress carries with it a responsibility to the Filipino people.

asr-000043
00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:52.680
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: The resources entrusted to this Office of the Ombudsman

asr-000044
00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:57.920
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: must therefore be utilized judiciously, efficiently,

asr-000045
00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:01.400
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: and with the highest standards of accountability.

asr-000046
00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:07.740
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: We trust that this Office will continue to use the support provided by Congress

asr-000047
00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:13.140
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: with the same zeal and dedication in carrying out its mandate

asr-000048
00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:18.740
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: and strengthening public confidence in the Ombudsman as the watchdog,

asr-000049
00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:25.180
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: I repeat, the watchdog of government, mobilizer for accountability,

asr-000050
00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:31.000
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: official critic of wrongdoing, and dispenser of justice.

asr-000051
00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:34.280
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Ultimately, our common objective is clear,

asr-000052
00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:36.680
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: to protect public funds,

asr-000053
00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:37.720
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: uphold equality,

asr-000054
00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:39.240
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: integrity in government,

asr-000055
00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:45.740
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: and ensure that the public office remains a service to the Filipino people.

asr-000056
00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:49.006
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: The Filipino people deserve no less.

asr-000057
00:05:49.107 --> 00:05:50.795
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Uh, thank you very much.

asr-000058
00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:55.520
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Now, we would like to ask the Office of the Ombudsman

asr-000059
00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:59.080
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: for the, the Ombudsman, uh,

asr-000060
00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:02.080
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: the Honorable Jesus Crispin “Boying” Remulla,

asr-000061
00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:05.543
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: you may now proceed with your presentation.

