Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Um, tungkol naman po sa regional reach ng Office of the Ombudsman,

asr-000318
00:26:35.230 --> 00:26:44.910
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ano po ang ano, how will your 2027 budget ensure that ma-expand natin po 'yung Ombudsman presence in the region

asr-000319
00:26:44.910 --> 00:26:47.590
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: and it becomes accessible to the region?

asr-000320
00:26:47.910 --> 00:26:57.280
Assistant Ombudsman Luis Gonzaga S. Bonoan, Jr.: Your Honor, actually, we are also looking at expanding

asr-000321
00:26:57.440 --> 00:27:02.220
Assistant Ombudsman Luis Gonzaga S. Bonoan, Jr.: our investigations and our reach to BARMM,

asr-000322
00:27:02.440 --> 00:27:05.700
Assistant Ombudsman Luis Gonzaga S. Bonoan, Jr.: to the Bangsamoro Autonomous Region in Muslim Mindanao.

asr-000323
00:27:06.320 --> 00:27:11.440
Assistant Ombudsman Luis Gonzaga S. Bonoan, Jr.: And also, we have also requested budgets for our different regional offices

asr-000324
00:27:11.440 --> 00:27:15.320
Assistant Ombudsman Luis Gonzaga S. Bonoan, Jr.: in Luzon, Visayas, Mindanao, as well as our satellite offices.

asr-000325
00:27:15.320 --> 00:27:22.220
Assistant Ombudsman Luis Gonzaga S. Bonoan, Jr.: This budget will ensure their accessibility to the public

asr-000326
00:27:22.220 --> 00:27:25.600
Assistant Ombudsman Luis Gonzaga S. Bonoan, Jr.: and continuous presence.

asr-000327
00:27:25.600 --> 00:27:25.880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yeah.

asr-000328
00:27:25.880 --> 00:27:27.799
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Do we have measurable indicators?

asr-000329
00:27:27.799 --> 00:27:32.559
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Perhaps mga numero na puwedeng magpatunay kung ilan ang nafa-file doon,

asr-000330
00:27:32.559 --> 00:27:36.320
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: and how—gaano po ka-efficient 'yung ating regional offices?

asr-000332
00:27:36.320 --> 00:27:38.080
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: If you don't have the data right now,

asr-000333
00:27:38.080 --> 00:27:41.640
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: we also appreciate, um, receiving the same from you,

asr-000334
00:27:41.640 --> 00:27:42.969
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: katulad po ng kanina.

asr-000335
00:27:44.039 --> 00:27:51.080
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ano po. Um, ah, siguro po 'yung huling question ko na lang po kay Ombudsman Remulla.

asr-000336
00:27:51.080 --> 00:27:56.039
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kamakailan po, um, naipahayag po ninyo at ako'y, uh,

asr-000337
00:27:56.039 --> 00:27:58.360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ang kinatawang ito ay nalungkot

asr-000338
00:27:58.360 --> 00:28:03.240
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: sa inyong pahayag na tama po ba na sinabi ninyo na wala na tayo—

asr-000339
00:28:03.240 --> 00:28:06.480
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ang taong bayan ay wala nang maaasahan sa DPWH?

asr-000340
00:28:06.480 --> 00:28:11.720
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ano po ba ang naging basehan ng statement po ninyo tungkol dito?

asr-000341
00:28:11.720 --> 00:28:14.200
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Ito po yung, salamat po sa tanong na yan,

asr-000342
00:28:14.200 --> 00:28:19.880
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: at maaari pong linawin ang konteksto ng aking pagsasabi niyan.

asr-000343
00:28:19.880 --> 00:28:25.537
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Pinag-uusapan po namin ang acquisition ng building, uh,

asr-000349
00:28:26.200 --> 00:28:33.340
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: ng NBI, kasi nga ako po yung dating Secretary of Justice

asr-000350
00:28:33.340 --> 00:28:36.360
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: at kabisado ko po yung mga nagiging problema

asr-000351
00:28:36.360 --> 00:28:43.060
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: sa pagpapagawa at pagtatalaga ng building ng gobyerno.

asr-000352
00:28:44.060 --> 00:28:47.500
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: At ang isa pong naging problema na nakita kong matindi

asr-000353
00:28:47.500 --> 00:28:50.420
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: ay yung Bureau of Immigration Building.

asr-000354
00:28:51.440 --> 00:28:56.020
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Inabot ho iyan halos ng walong bilyon at labindalawang taon,

asr-000355
00:28:56.020 --> 00:29:00.040
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: at hanggang ngayon, ngayon lang yata na tapos,

asr-000356
00:29:00.820 --> 00:29:03.020
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: yung driveway papunta po sa parking lot niya.

asr-000357
00:29:03.900 --> 00:29:05.560
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Yung driveway po niya, hindi ho kakasya.

asr-000358
00:29:05.940 --> 00:29:07.860
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Ang kakasya lang po, Wigo.

asr-000359
00:29:08.420 --> 00:29:09.940
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Yung maliit po na sasakyan,

asr-000360
00:29:10.620 --> 00:29:12.720
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: pag may dala kayong pickup o SUV,

asr-000361
00:29:13.360 --> 00:29:16.380
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: hindi na po kakasya at hindi na po makakaparada sa taas.

asr-000362
00:29:17.300 --> 00:29:18.720
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Ang problema po kasi,

asr-000363
00:29:19.680 --> 00:29:21.860
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: pag may government building na ginagawa,

asr-000364
00:29:22.620 --> 00:29:25.780
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: alam naman natin na hindi ho madali magpatayo ng building.

asr-000365
00:29:26.020 --> 00:29:28.780
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Ito yung building, maraming pong cost overrun yan.

asr-000366
00:29:29.340 --> 00:29:31.340
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Pero pag ito po tinamaan ng graft

asr-000367
00:29:31.340 --> 00:29:35.180
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: at tinamaan ng kickback mentality,

asr-000368
00:29:36.100 --> 00:29:39.060
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: talaga po mauubos pati yung building at mauubos po yung driveway.

asr-000369
00:29:39.800 --> 00:29:44.320
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Ganoon kasama ang nakita kong pangyayari sa akin pong karanasan.

asr-000370
00:29:44.860 --> 00:29:47.280
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Dito po sa gobyerno, matagal na po ako sa gobyerno.

asr-000371
00:29:47.880 --> 00:29:50.860
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Nagsimula po ako sa gobyerno 1992.

asr-000372
00:29:50.860 --> 00:29:56.000
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: At hindi naman po tuloy-tuloy, pero kadalasan po yan.

asr-000373
00:29:56.020 --> 00:29:59.020
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Hanggang 2026, halos sa gobyerno po ako.

asr-000374
00:30:00.080 --> 00:30:12.820
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Nakita ko lahat ng pangyayari sa paggastos ng pera ng bayan, at ang pagpapagawa ng building, isa po sa pinakanakakamuhi pong nangyayari sa atin.

asr-000375
00:30:12.940 --> 00:30:24.720
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Nakakaawa po 'yung ating mga—lagay natin sa paaralan pa lamang, ang paaralan po ng mga bata na kaunting-kaunti na ang ginawa, halos ang sama ng standard.

asr-000376
00:30:24.720 --> 00:30:39.200
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Pero itong mga building po na talagang kinakailangan ng gobyerno, talagang pagka nagpatayo po tayo at may [unclear] po sa pagpapatayo ng building, talaga pong naging substandard po talaga ang building.

asr-000377
00:30:39.900 --> 00:30:48.780
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Ayun nga, example ho niyan, Immigration Building sa Macapagal Boulevard na dapat ho napakaganda kung titingnan natin ang naging gastos.

asr-000378
00:30:49.040 --> 00:30:54.260
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Halos walong bilyon ang aking pagkakaunawa. Pero kung titingnan ko ho at i-value ninyo ngayon,

asr-000379
00:30:54.720 --> 00:30:59.160
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: sa ngayong merkado, kung magkano po 'yung building na 'yon, baka hindi ho umabot ng two billion.

asr-000380
00:31:00.360 --> 00:31:03.120
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Kaya ang laki po ng ano, ng sayang eh.

asr-000381
00:31:03.640 --> 00:31:12.540
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Yun po, probably, it’s a point of emphasis na kinakailangan pong bantayan natin ang kaban ng bayan pagdating po sa pagpapatayo ng mga gusali.

asr-000382
00:31:13.860 --> 00:31:17.660
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Ombudsman. I share your observations and frustration.

asr-000383
00:31:18.240 --> 00:31:22.860
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, given that po, ano po ang maaaring maitulong ng Ombudsman?

asr-000384
00:31:22.860 --> 00:31:35.260
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Given yung ganyang observation ninyo, upang linisin natin ang ahensyang ito ng katiwalian, without preempting whatever investigation you are currently doing right now, kung meron po,

asr-000385
00:31:35.660 --> 00:31:43.840
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Para po, maging dekalidad yung ating mga infrastruktura at maibalik natin ang kumpiyansa ng taong bayan sa ahensya.

asr-000386
00:31:44.840 --> 00:31:51.080
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Unang-una siguro, kung talagang DPWH ang pag-uusapan, dapat ho ginagamit natin ang RDC.

asr-000387
00:31:51.080 --> 00:31:53.960
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Lahat po ng proyekto, dapat po nakaplano.

asr-000388
00:31:54.480 --> 00:31:58.800
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Hindi ho puwedeng, “Bigyan mo ako ng listahan ng gagawin mong kalye, tapos ako nang bahala.”

asr-000389
00:31:59.060 --> 00:31:59.780
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Hindi po ganun eh.

asr-000390
00:32:00.220 --> 00:32:01.280
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Dapat ho yan nakaplano.

asr-000391
00:32:01.820 --> 00:32:07.400
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Ang laki po ng gobyerno natin, marami tayong gobyerno na gumagawa ng trabaho para planuhin na maayos ang lahat.

asr-000392
00:32:08.200 --> 00:32:09.760
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Pero hindi po dapat ganun ah.

asr-000393
00:32:10.180 --> 00:32:15.520
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Dapat po talaga deliberate tayo at every step of the way sa paggastos ng pera ng bayan.

asr-000394
00:32:15.920 --> 00:32:18.080
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Yun nga 'yung nagiging problema natin,

asr-000395
00:32:18.080 --> 00:32:23.640
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: yung ating mga regional development plans, parang hindi ho nasunod nung bandang huli.

asr-000396
00:32:23.920 --> 00:32:28.780
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Itong mga nakaraang taon, lahat po naging flood-control budget na lang.

asr-000397
00:32:29.500 --> 00:32:40.980
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Ang nangyari po sa budget natin, yung mga sabihin natin, flagship project ng Pangulo, nawala, naging unprogrammed fund na lang.

asr-000398
00:32:41.600 --> 00:32:44.940
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Yung po ating foreign-assisted project, naging unprogrammed na lang.

asr-000399
00:32:44.940 --> 00:32:47.900
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Kaya ang aming pong gagawin dito,

asr-000400
00:32:48.080 --> 00:32:54.880
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: sa aming opisina, magtatayo ho kami ng isang committee na babantayan lamang ang budget

asr-000401
00:32:54.880 --> 00:32:57.860
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: at kung paano ho ginagastos ang pera ng bayan,

asr-000402
00:32:58.320 --> 00:33:02.860
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: na pwede na rin ho maging sumbungan ng taong bayan kung meron pong pagmamalabis.

asr-000403
00:33:03.620 --> 00:33:09.340
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: So, yung pagbabantay po ng budget, isa na ho sa direct functions namin, ang tingin ko na pinakamahalaga.

asr-000404
00:33:11.020 --> 00:33:12.900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Maraming salamat po, Ombudsman.

asr-000405
00:33:12.960 --> 00:33:14.160
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: I still have a little time.

asr-000406
00:33:14.160 --> 00:33:16.300
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Let me just siguro state that,

asr-000407
00:33:16.300 --> 00:33:26.640
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ang kinatawang ito po ay kaisa ninyo sa inyong hangarin upang palakasin muli ang tiwala ng taong bayan sa ahensya.

asr-000408
00:33:27.060 --> 00:33:33.600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: At alam po natin, nasabi nyo po sa inyong closing statement sa presentation, yung impact ng corruption.

asr-000409
00:33:34.120 --> 00:33:43.320
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And umaasa po kami na tunay na ang opisina ng Ombudsman ay ang magiging watchdog, mobilizer, official critic, and dispenser of justice.

asr-000410
00:33:43.320 --> 00:33:43.960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: At ako

asr-000411
00:33:43.960 --> 00:33:52.120
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: po'y naniniwala din na sa huling phrase ng inyong presentation, that the Filipino people deserve no less.

asr-000412
00:33:52.120 --> 00:33:53.679
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Maraming salamat po, Mr. Chair.

asr-000413
00:33:53.679 --> 00:33:55.039
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Maraming salamat po.

asr-000414
00:33:55.039 --> 00:33:58.120
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you, Representative Iris Montes.

asr-000415
00:33:58.120 --> 00:34:06.783
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Before we proceed to the next interpellator, may I now acknowledge the arrival of Representative Karl Fernandez Legazpi.

asr-000416
00:34:08.774 --> 00:34:12.284
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: We have Representative Mark Anthony Santos.

asr-000418
00:34:13.955 --> 00:34:18.224
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: We have Assistant Minority Leader Robert Nazal.

asr-000419
00:34:19.777 --> 00:34:25.615
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And Deputy Minority Leader Antonio Tinio.

asr-000420
00:34:26.645 --> 00:34:27.252
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Tony.

asr-000421
00:34:27.691 --> 00:34:28.400
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And one more.

asr-000422
00:34:29.918 --> 00:34:34.000
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And we have Representative Franz Pumaren.

asr-000423
00:34:34.000 --> 00:34:34.340
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Welcome.

asr-000424
00:34:34.947 --> 00:34:38.255
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So we now go to the second interpellator.

asr-000425
00:34:38.795 --> 00:34:40.839
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: He will belong to the independent.

asr-000426
00:34:40.839 --> 00:34:43.402
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: We have minority, independent, majority.

asr-000427
00:34:43.874 --> 00:34:44.667
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Congressman.

asr-000428
00:34:45.325 --> 00:34:47.840
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And then, Toby Tiangco is now recognized.

asr-000429
00:34:49.257 --> 00:34:50.084
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-000430
00:34:50.405 --> 00:34:53.037
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Uh, Mr. Chair, um, wala po akong tanong.

asr-000431
00:34:53.290 --> 00:34:57.480
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Um, I just want to manifest that I support the budget of the Office of the Ombudsman.

asr-000432
00:34:57.480 --> 00:35:02.680
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Especially, Mr. Chair, the amendments that they are requesting for the general provisions, no?

asr-000433
00:35:02.680 --> 00:35:05.035
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: And I'm sure, uh, you will be one with me.

asr-000434
00:35:05.356 --> 00:35:06.824
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: We've known each other very well.

asr-000435
00:35:07.162 --> 00:35:11.079
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Um, because yung Office of the Ombudsman is part of the CFAG,

asr-000436
00:35:11.079 --> 00:35:15.599
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: the, um, uh, Constitutional Fiscal Autonomy Group, no.

asr-000437
00:35:15.835 --> 00:35:23.902
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: So I hope that the, um, amendments to the special provisions will also be applicable to the other members of the CFAG.

asr-000438
00:35:24.273 --> 00:35:27.216
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Hindi lang po doon sa Office of the Ombudsman.

asr-000439
00:35:27.440 --> 00:35:32.440
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Um, sana po we make it applicable to the Commission on Elections,

asr-000440
00:35:32.440 --> 00:35:37.216
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: to the Civil Service Commission, to the Commission on Audit, and the Commission on Human Rights.

asr-000441
00:35:37.942 --> 00:35:42.363
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: And this was my, um, ito po advocacy ko since 2013, eh.

asr-000442
00:35:42.818 --> 00:35:44.599
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: I was already supporting their fiscal autonomy.

asr-000443
00:35:45.119 --> 00:35:47.453
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: So I'm surprised that it's still an issue right now, no?

asr-000444
00:35:47.880 --> 00:35:48.440
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: So yun lang po.

asr-000445
00:35:48.440 --> 00:35:53.319
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: And I hope at the proper time, the Chairman will be the one to introduce the amendments in the floor.

asr-000446
00:35:53.319 --> 00:35:54.158
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Thank you very much, Mr. Chair.

asr-000447
00:35:54.158 --> 00:35:56.359
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you, Representative Toby Tiangco.

asr-000448
00:35:56.359 --> 00:36:01.359
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you for your full support for the budget of the Ombudsman.

asr-000449
00:36:01.359 --> 00:36:03.240
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And of course, also the special provisions.

asr-000450
00:36:04.359 --> 00:36:07.372
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: The other commissions are also having that already.

asr-000451
00:36:07.422 --> 00:36:08.992
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: The COMELEC and the others.

asr-000452
00:36:09.397 --> 00:36:11.319
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Civil Service and COA.

asr-000453
00:36:11.319 --> 00:36:14.880
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: But the focus now is the Ombudsman.

asr-000454
00:36:14.880 --> 00:36:19.119
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: We agree with you, and we support you in the special provisions for the Ombudsman.

asr-000455
00:36:20.040 --> 00:36:21.680
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So that is the stand of the Chair.

asr-000456
00:36:22.560 --> 00:36:24.839
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Uh, we have to get the approval of everyone here.

asr-000457
00:36:25.480 --> 00:36:27.453
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: But, uh, thank you for your proposal.

asr-000458
00:36:27.554 --> 00:36:27.908
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Yes.

asr-000459
00:36:29.022 --> 00:36:33.800
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Yung doon sa savings, use of income, retirement benefits,

asr-000460
00:36:33.800 --> 00:36:37.105
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: and sana isama na rin po natin yung validity of appropriations.

asr-000461
00:36:38.860 --> 00:36:43.062
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: We will have that language recommended to the plenary.

asr-000462
00:36:43.520 --> 00:36:44.079
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you very much.

asr-000463
00:36:44.240 --> 00:36:44.950
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Thank you very much, Mr. Chair.

asr-000464
00:36:45.200 --> 00:36:47.839
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you, Congressman Toby Tiangco.

asr-000465
00:36:47.839 --> 00:36:49.492
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Now we go to the majority.

asr-000466
00:36:50.119 --> 00:36:52.867
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And we have the representative from Baguio.

asr-000467
00:36:53.599 --> 00:36:56.680
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: The Honorable Representative Mauricio Domogan.

asr-000468
00:36:58.680 --> 00:37:07.582
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Thank you, Mr. Chairman, Apo, Ombudsman, and the members of the family of the Ombudsman.

asr-000469
00:37:08.800 --> 00:37:11.733
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: First, I join.

asr-000471
00:37:13.400 --> 00:37:20.119
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Of course, Congressman Tiangco and the others, fully supporting,

asr-000472
00:37:20.119 --> 00:37:24.592
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: including the proposed amendments of the budget of the Ombudsman.

asr-000473
00:37:25.119 --> 00:37:27.292
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: We have some few questions.

asr-000474
00:37:29.440 --> 00:37:33.940
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: During the hearing on the Committee on Justice on the Impeachment,

asr-000475
00:37:35.319 --> 00:37:42.901
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Witness Ramil Madriaga came out with two names.

asr-000476
00:37:43.520 --> 00:37:46.917
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: One of them happens to be with the Ombudsman.

asr-000477
00:37:48.119 --> 00:37:49.685
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Maybe we know what happened to that.

asr-000478
00:37:55.240 --> 00:37:59.590
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Ombudsman Remulla, please respond to the query of Congressman Domogan.

asr-000479
00:38:00.359 --> 00:38:03.117
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Yes, thank you, Your Honor.

asr-000480
00:38:03.920 --> 00:38:12.400
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: The Internal Affairs Bureau of the Ombudsman is now on the case of Mr. Madriaga, of what was mentioned by Mr. Madriaga.

asr-000481
00:38:12.400 --> 00:38:18.240
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And that we already had the show-cause order issued to the person referred to by Mr. Madriaga.

asr-000482
00:38:18.240 --> 00:38:19.680
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And he has already answered.

asr-000483
00:38:19.680 --> 00:38:26.880
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: So, the IAB is now pursuing, the Internal Affairs Bureau is pursuing the case to its proper logical conclusion.

asr-000484
00:38:26.880 --> 00:38:27.603
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Thank you, Your Honor.

asr-000485
00:38:28.160 --> 00:38:29.881
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you, Representative Domogan.

asr-000486
00:38:30.280 --> 00:38:32.319
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Thank you, Chairman.

asr-000487
00:38:32.680 --> 00:38:33.610
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Next.

asr-000488
00:38:36.400 --> 00:38:44.359
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: From your records, how many had been received by your office?

asr-000489
00:38:44.359 --> 00:38:45.960
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: complaints

asr-000490
00:38:45.960 --> 00:38:46.960
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: involving

asr-000491
00:38:46.960 --> 00:38:55.109
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Having conflict interest of incumbent officials of government,

asr-000492
00:38:56.000 --> 00:38:57.556
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: particularly congressmen and senators?

asr-000493
00:39:02.079 --> 00:39:03.023
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Do you have records?

asr-000494
00:39:05.240 --> 00:39:11.720
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Your Honor, there aren't many complaints when it comes to conflict of interest.

asr-000495
00:39:11.720 --> 00:39:17.079
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It is something motu proprio that we start the investigations of the conflict of interest.

asr-000496
00:39:17.079 --> 00:39:30.901
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Probably, one reason is because I've been, I was a member of this house for four terms, and actually, I was elected to five terms, and I was very aware of the conflict of interest emanating at that time.

asr-000497
00:39:31.640 --> 00:39:40.604
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But, as a member of the house, we know the culture here is that, well, if I may be a little more informal in my words, walang basagan ng trip.

asr-000498
00:39:41.760 --> 00:39:46.200
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But, Your Honor, I have been given a constitutional duty to check on

asr-000499
00:39:46.200 --> 00:39:46.599
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: conflicts

asr-000500
00:39:46.599 --> 00:39:46.839
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: of

asr-000501
00:39:46.839 --> 00:39:48.240
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: interest and

asr-000502
00:39:48.240 --> 00:39:48.960
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: graft and corruption.

asr-000503
00:39:48.960 --> 00:39:53.319
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: That's why I think that that knowledge came to me very handily.

asr-000504
00:39:53.319 --> 00:39:56.787
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And, that's where the motu proprio started.

asr-000505
00:39:57.319 --> 00:40:04.800
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But there are other, there are other people who give us information that do not necessarily file complaints.

asr-000506
00:40:04.800 --> 00:40:07.250
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But, we use this to start investigations, Your Honor.

asr-000507
00:40:09.839 --> 00:40:10.844
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-000508
00:40:11.720 --> 00:40:17.400
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you, Representative Domogan and our Ombudsman.

asr-000509
00:40:17.400 --> 00:40:19.720
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: We go now to—back to—

asr-000510
00:40:19.720 --> 00:40:20.319
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Not yet finished.

asr-000511
00:40:20.319 --> 00:40:21.079
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: I'm not yet finished.

asr-000511-split-2
00:40:21.079 --> 00:40:21.920
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Please proceed.

asr-000512
00:40:21.920 --> 00:40:24.790
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: You still have 3 minutes and 32 seconds.

asr-000513
00:40:24.800 --> 00:40:25.897
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: I thought you're finished.

asr-000514
00:40:26.599 --> 00:40:27.044
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: I'm sorry.

asr-000515
00:40:28.760 --> 00:40:30.520
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: No problem, Mr. Chairman.

asr-000516
00:40:32.160 --> 00:40:38.958
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Now, talking of these problems of corruption, which is appearing to be number one in our country today,

asr-000517
00:40:40.800 --> 00:40:45.168
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: relative specifically to government projects,

asr-000518
00:40:47.480 --> 00:40:53.487
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: I noticed that the requirement of pre-audit had been removed.

asr-000519
00:40:58.280 --> 00:41:00.085
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: That was in 2011.

asr-000520
00:41:01.520 --> 00:41:03.157
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: That was in 2011.

asr-000521
00:41:04.880 --> 00:41:07.679
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Because when pre-audit was being followed,

asr-000522
00:41:09.040 --> 00:41:16.599
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: well, my seatmate here, who happens to be the regional director of the Cordillera,

asr-000523
00:41:16.599 --> 00:41:23.319
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: when we rehabilitated the city of Baguio from the ruins of the killer earthquake of 1990,

asr-000524
00:41:23.319 --> 00:41:24.841
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: wala namang red flag eh.

asr-000525
00:41:25.440 --> 00:41:28.317
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Kasi kailangan ninyong pre-audit.

asr-000526
00:41:28.839 --> 00:41:30.629
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Now, may we get your view.

asr-000527
00:41:31.240 --> 00:41:41.564
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Do you support us with the bill that we make as mandatory for payment of government projects,

asr-000528
00:41:42.119 --> 00:41:46.119
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: pre-audit coupled with geomapping of the seed projects?

asr-000529
00:41:46.119 --> 00:41:47.720
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: So that, klaro, na nandiyan.

asr-000530
00:41:47.720 --> 00:41:52.240
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Siguro, kung may lulusot pa na ghost project,

asr-000531
00:41:52.240 --> 00:41:59.232
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: hindi ko na alam kung mayroon pa kung pre-audit complemented by geomapping.

asr-000532
00:42:00.200 --> 00:42:02.084
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It would be a big help, Your Honor.

asr-000533
00:42:02.880 --> 00:42:05.155
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: However, that's already the province of the COA.

asr-000534
00:42:05.359 --> 00:42:11.956
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And I believe that probably COA should be able to address that issue.

asr-000535
00:42:12.400 --> 00:42:15.040
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And maybe they will best lead more personnel.

asr-000536
00:42:15.040 --> 00:42:20.760
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Because they're always, the limitation of COA, as far as I'm concerned,

asr-000537
00:42:20.760 --> 00:42:23.680
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: as far as I've heard, is that they lack the people.

asr-000538
00:42:23.680 --> 00:42:27.329
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Maybe they need a bigger complement of people to do the job, Your Honor.

asr-000539
00:42:29.280 --> 00:42:31.079
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Thank you, Apo, Ombudsman.

asr-000540
00:42:31.079 --> 00:42:36.610
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: We brought this with COA, and they fully support it, only they want additional personnel.

asr-000541
00:42:37.680 --> 00:42:39.559
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Tama po iyong sabi mo.

asr-000542
00:42:39.559 --> 00:42:42.770
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: So, we hope that the bill that we did file,

asr-000543
00:42:43.760 --> 00:42:44.525
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: should,

asr-000544
00:42:46.680 --> 00:42:47.400
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: be passed.

asr-000545
00:42:47.400 --> 00:42:55.628
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Because I am confident that this can be a good weapon against this ghost project

asr-000546
00:42:58.440 --> 00:43:00.269
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: happening in our country today.

asr-000547
00:43:07.520 --> 00:43:10.520
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Next.

asr-000548
00:43:10.520 --> 00:43:13.020
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: The complaints that have been filed with your good office,

asr-000549
00:43:13.020 --> 00:43:15.440
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Apo, Ombudsman,

asr-000550
00:43:15.440 --> 00:43:17.040
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: how long it will take?

asr-000551
00:43:17.040 --> 00:43:22.679
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Because usually, there's a period for the conduct of the preliminary investigation,

asr-000552
00:43:23.160 --> 00:43:23.880
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: everything.

asr-000553
00:43:23.880 --> 00:43:26.881
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: How long it will take to be processed?

asr-000554
00:43:28.960 --> 00:43:34.087
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Sir, the first stage that we undertake here is fact-finding.

asr-000555
00:43:35.920 --> 00:43:38.960
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: And how many days of fact-finding? Thirty days? Sixty days?

asr-000556
00:43:38.960 --> 00:43:42.359
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Which is 30 days for non-complex cases,

asr-000557
00:43:42.359 --> 00:43:45.440
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and 60 days for more complex cases.

asr-000558
00:43:45.440 --> 00:43:47.671
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And then we have preliminary investigation,

asr-000559
00:43:48.000 --> 00:43:50.400
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: which is another 60 days.

asr-000560
00:43:50.400 --> 00:43:52.400
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: 30 to 60 days, Your Honor.

asr-000561
00:43:52.400 --> 00:43:54.119
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: 60 days maximum.

asr-000562
00:43:54.119 --> 00:43:59.146
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: So, right now, we already put in tighter deadlines to do our work.

asr-000563
00:43:59.480 --> 00:44:04.520
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And we just hired 60 more lawyers, Your Honor.

asr-000564
00:44:04.520 --> 00:44:07.800
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: This year, we've hired 60 lawyers,

asr-000565
00:44:07.800 --> 00:44:11.040
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and we will be hiring 40 more for the year,

asr-000566
00:44:11.040 --> 00:44:12.920
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: for a total of 100 lawyers,

asr-000567
00:44:12.920 --> 00:44:16.319
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: to help us meet that kind of deadline,

asr-000568
00:44:16.319 --> 00:44:19.079
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: because it can be very stringent on those

asr-000569
00:44:19.079 --> 00:44:20.932
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: conducting the investigations, Your Honor.

asr-000570
00:44:22.720 --> 00:44:24.400
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Thank you, Apo, Ombudsman.

asr-000571
00:44:24.400 --> 00:44:27.850
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Well, I brought this up because I know of some cases

asr-000572
00:44:28.920 --> 00:44:30.432
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: which are still pending there,

asr-000573
00:44:30.960 --> 00:44:32.035
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: that had been filed

asr-000574
00:44:32.500 --> 00:44:34.500
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: some time

asr-000575
00:44:34.500 --> 00:44:37.280
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: ago.

asr-000576
00:44:37.280 --> 00:44:37.756
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Anyway,

asr-000577
00:44:38.400 --> 00:44:39.612
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: we totally support,

asr-000578
00:44:40.559 --> 00:44:41.232
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: as we said,

asr-000579
00:44:41.960 --> 00:44:44.540
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: your budget, including the proposed amendment.

asr-000580
00:44:45.160 --> 00:44:45.535
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: So,

asr-000581
00:44:46.880 --> 00:44:47.459
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: and,

asr-000582
00:44:48.640 --> 00:44:49.282
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: we commend

asr-000583
00:44:50.040 --> 00:44:52.943
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: the tenacity of our present Ombudsman

asr-000584
00:44:53.319 --> 00:44:54.108
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: to really

asr-000585
00:44:54.800 --> 00:44:56.048
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: go after those

asr-000586
00:44:56.960 --> 00:44:58.280
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: involved.

asr-000587
00:44:58.280 --> 00:45:02.480
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: in anomalies within your jurisdiction.

asr-000588
00:45:02.480 --> 00:45:04.480
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Thank you, Apo Ombudsman and the family.

asr-000589
00:45:04.480 --> 00:45:06.119
Rep. Mauricio G. Domogan: Thank you, Apo Chairman.

asr-000590
00:45:06.119 --> 00:45:07.390
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you, Your Honor.

asr-000591
00:45:07.400 --> 00:45:09.110
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you, Congressman Domogan.

asr-000592
00:45:09.640 --> 00:45:10.831
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Next in the list.

asr-000593
00:45:11.920 --> 00:45:14.425
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Before that, let me just recognize

asr-000594
00:45:14.920 --> 00:45:16.535
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Congressman Edgar Erice.

asr-000595
00:45:17.359 --> 00:45:18.307
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you for coming.

asr-000596
00:45:19.000 --> 00:45:20.109
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Who else?

