00:45:25.640 --> 00:45:27.368
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: the next interpellator.

asr-000601
00:45:27.920 --> 00:45:32.768
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: We have, yeah, from the majority-minority,

asr-000602
00:45:33.400 --> 00:45:35.401
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Representative Chel Diokno.

asr-000603
00:45:37.440 --> 00:45:38.990
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: Thank you, Chair Rufus.

asr-000604
00:45:39.000 --> 00:45:41.069
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: Magandang umaga po, Ombudsman Remulla

asr-000605
00:45:41.079 --> 00:45:43.349
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: at sa lahat ng taga-Ombudsman.

asr-000606
00:45:43.359 --> 00:45:45.155
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: At sa mga kasamahan din po natin.

asr-000607
00:45:45.839 --> 00:45:48.270
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: I totally agree with your statement earlier

asr-000608
00:45:48.280 --> 00:45:50.470
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: that the people deserve the best,

asr-000609
00:45:50.480 --> 00:45:52.445
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: especially when it comes to anti-corruption.

asr-000610
00:45:53.760 --> 00:45:55.829
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: And I know that the Office of the Ombudsman

asr-000611
00:45:55.839 --> 00:45:58.150
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: is just one of several agencies

asr-000612
00:45:58.160 --> 00:45:59.470
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: that is,

asr-000613
00:45:59.480 --> 00:46:01.030
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: really, dapat nakatutok

asr-000614
00:46:01.040 --> 00:46:03.790
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: pagdating sa isyong ito.

asr-000615
00:46:03.800 --> 00:46:05.309
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: I'd like to share something

asr-000616
00:46:05.319 --> 00:46:06.470
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: with the Ombudsman

asr-000617
00:46:06.480 --> 00:46:09.109
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: that perhaps you're not aware of.

asr-000618
00:46:09.119 --> 00:46:10.549
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: About 20 years ago,

asr-000619
00:46:10.559 --> 00:46:13.083
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: I was provided with a copy of a study

asr-000620
00:46:13.720 --> 00:46:15.790
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: that was submitted to your office

asr-000621
00:46:15.800 --> 00:46:17.309
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: which showed that

asr-000622
00:46:17.319 --> 00:46:20.069
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: out of 110 persons

asr-000623
00:46:20.079 --> 00:46:23.073
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: convicted of graft and corruption offenses,

asr-000624
00:46:24.359 --> 00:46:24.910
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: sasampu lang po

asr-000625
00:46:24.920 --> 00:46:26.667
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: ang actually nakakulong.

asr-000626
00:46:27.400 --> 00:46:28.829
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: These refer to convictions

asr-000627
00:46:28.839 --> 00:46:28.990
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: already,

asr-000628
00:46:29.000 --> 00:46:30.886
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: already by final judgment.

asr-000629
00:46:31.280 --> 00:46:32.630
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: And one of the recommendations

asr-000630
00:46:32.640 --> 00:46:33.750
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: of that study,

asr-000631
00:46:33.760 --> 00:46:35.030
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: I can provide you with a copy.

asr-000632
00:46:35.040 --> 00:46:36.269
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: I still have a copy, sir.

asr-000633
00:46:36.839 --> 00:46:38.530
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: Is that the government

asr-000634
00:46:39.240 --> 00:46:42.040
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: create a centralized system

asr-000635
00:46:42.480 --> 00:46:45.549
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: for ensuring that those convicted,

asr-000636
00:46:45.559 --> 00:46:48.390
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: especially those who appeal their convictions,

asr-000637
00:46:48.400 --> 00:46:50.990
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: actually serve their sentences.

asr-000638
00:46:51.000 --> 00:46:51.950
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: As I understand it,

asr-000639
00:46:51.960 --> 00:46:52.510
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: as of now,

asr-000640
00:46:52.520 --> 00:46:56.230
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: there is no such system in place.

asr-000641
00:46:56.240 --> 00:46:58.169
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: What may I know your stand,

asr-000642
00:46:58.179 --> 00:46:59.030
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: Ombudsman Remulla,

asr-000643
00:46:59.040 --> 00:47:00.790
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: on this and what can we do

asr-000644
00:47:00.800 --> 00:47:02.910
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: to move forward with this proposal

asr-000645
00:47:02.920 --> 00:47:04.829
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: that has already been on the table

asr-000646
00:47:04.839 --> 00:47:06.560
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: for more than 20 years?

asr-000647
00:47:09.480 --> 00:47:10.150
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Your Honor,

asr-000648
00:47:10.160 --> 00:47:11.750
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: our legal system is one

asr-000649
00:47:11.760 --> 00:47:13.430
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: which is not very clear

asr-000650
00:47:13.440 --> 00:47:15.309
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: when it comes to people

asr-000651
00:47:15.319 --> 00:47:17.230
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: who have been sentenced

asr-000652
00:47:17.240 --> 00:47:19.170
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: by the Anti-Graft Court

asr-000653
00:47:19.180 --> 00:47:20.212
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: or by any lower court.

asr-000654
00:47:21.400 --> 00:47:21.578
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Usually,

asr-000655
00:47:23.060 --> 00:47:24.700
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: people are still allowed to post bail

asr-000656
00:47:25.240 --> 00:47:26.590
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: after they've been sentenced.

asr-000657
00:47:28.160 --> 00:47:29.390
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But I think there are

asr-000658
00:47:29.400 --> 00:47:32.150
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: this has to be

asr-000659
00:47:32.160 --> 00:47:32.902
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: redefined in our times.

asr-000660
00:47:34.440 --> 00:47:36.158
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: We have to make people face the music

asr-000661
00:47:36.640 --> 00:47:37.762
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: that once convicted,

asr-000662
00:47:38.880 --> 00:47:40.208
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: you serve your sentence immediately

asr-000663
00:47:42.040 --> 00:47:44.670
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and only the appeal can stop

asr-000664
00:47:44.680 --> 00:47:45.950
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: the service of your sentence.

asr-000665
00:47:45.960 --> 00:47:46.537
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Let's say,

asr-000666
00:47:48.599 --> 00:47:50.671
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: one is sentenced by original trial court

asr-000667
00:47:51.599 --> 00:47:53.589
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: for homicide,

asr-000668
00:47:53.599 --> 00:47:54.974
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: which is a bailable offense.

asr-000669
00:47:56.200 --> 00:47:57.390
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: The presumption is the court

asr-000670
00:47:57.400 --> 00:47:58.619
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: already did the right thing.

asr-000671
00:47:59.359 --> 00:48:00.273
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But because,

asr-000672
00:48:00.599 --> 00:48:02.069
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: we allow them to post bail

asr-000673
00:48:02.079 --> 00:48:03.390
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: after conviction

asr-000674
00:48:03.400 --> 00:48:04.778
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: in the appellate process,

asr-000675
00:48:05.680 --> 00:48:07.670
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: there is no time determined.

asr-000676
00:48:07.680 --> 00:48:09.349
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: There's no time for this

asr-000677
00:48:09.359 --> 00:48:10.263
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: to mature into

asr-000678
00:48:12.880 --> 00:48:14.150
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: something that has to be served

asr-000679
00:48:14.160 --> 00:48:15.899
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: by the person sentenced.

asr-000680
00:48:16.200 --> 00:48:17.190
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: So, the appellate process

asr-000681
00:48:17.200 --> 00:48:19.109
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: is very defective, Your Honor.

asr-000682
00:48:19.119 --> 00:48:19.829
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: There is no time,

asr-000683
00:48:19.839 --> 00:48:20.710
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: there's no timetable

asr-000684
00:48:20.720 --> 00:48:22.230
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: for the appellate process.

asr-000685
00:48:22.240 --> 00:48:23.932
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: You go to the Court of Appeals

asr-000686
00:48:24.319 --> 00:48:25.390
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and then the Supreme Court,

asr-000687
00:48:25.400 --> 00:48:26.699
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: then we don't know what will happen.

asr-000688
00:48:27.400 --> 00:48:29.602
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: So, are we going to allow

asr-000689
00:48:30.079 --> 00:48:30.990
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: people to post bail

asr-000690
00:48:31.000 --> 00:48:32.069
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: after they've been convicted

asr-000691
00:48:32.079 --> 00:48:33.150
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: or are we going to let them

asr-000692
00:48:33.160 --> 00:48:34.430
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: serve their sentence?

asr-000693
00:48:34.440 --> 00:48:36.870
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I think that's the critical thing

asr-000694
00:48:36.880 --> 00:48:38.069
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: that there's an elephant in the room

asr-000695
00:48:38.079 --> 00:48:40.270
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: that we have to ask

asr-000696
00:48:40.280 --> 00:48:42.190
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: the Supreme Court about

asr-000697
00:48:42.200 --> 00:48:45.390
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: because it's wasting

asr-000698
00:48:45.400 --> 00:48:46.730
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: our government resources

asr-000699
00:48:47.680 --> 00:48:49.270
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: if we do not actually implement

asr-000700
00:48:49.280 --> 00:48:50.712
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: these decisions immediately.

asr-000701
00:48:51.400 --> 00:48:52.870
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: So, the immediate implementation

asr-000702
00:48:52.880 --> 00:48:53.870
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: of decisions, I think,

asr-000703
00:48:53.880 --> 00:48:56.150
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: is one of the best ways

asr-000704
00:48:56.160 --> 00:48:59.150
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: to make sure that people

asr-000705
00:48:59.160 --> 00:48:59.390
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: will live,

asr-000706
00:48:59.400 --> 00:49:00.854
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: will not do the offense again

asr-000707
00:49:01.200 --> 00:49:02.913
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: because unless they serve sentence

asr-000708
00:49:03.839 --> 00:49:05.630
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and they are put behind bars

asr-000709
00:49:05.640 --> 00:49:06.288
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: immediately,

asr-000710
00:49:06.920 --> 00:49:07.750
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: people will forget

asr-000711
00:49:07.760 --> 00:49:09.150
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: that they have been convicted

asr-000712
00:49:09.160 --> 00:49:10.000
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: after a while.

asr-000713
00:49:10.440 --> 00:49:12.030
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: So, it's something that we have to face

asr-000714
00:49:12.040 --> 00:49:12.937
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: as a country.

asr-000715
00:49:13.319 --> 00:49:14.190
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Maybe we have to ask

asr-000716
00:49:14.200 --> 00:49:14.789
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: the Supreme Court

asr-000717
00:49:14.799 --> 00:49:15.907
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: the same question, Your Honor.

asr-000718
00:49:16.680 --> 00:49:17.746
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: Tama po kayo, O Ombudsman.

asr-000719
00:49:18.480 --> 00:49:20.589
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: And I believe...

asr-000720
00:49:20.599 --> 00:49:21.610
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Chel, I'd just like to

asr-000721
00:49:22.520 --> 00:49:23.829
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: also remind the Ombudsman

asr-000722
00:49:23.839 --> 00:49:25.910
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: that the presumption of innocence

asr-000723
00:49:25.920 --> 00:49:27.331
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: is in the Constitution.

asr-000724
00:49:27.920 --> 00:49:29.052
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Even the Supreme Court

asr-000725
00:49:29.880 --> 00:49:31.145
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: will not be able

asr-000726
00:49:31.680 --> 00:49:33.136
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: to decree

asr-000727
00:49:33.680 --> 00:49:35.630
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: that upon conviction

asr-000728
00:49:35.640 --> 00:49:36.910
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: in the RTC,

asr-000729
00:49:36.920 --> 00:49:39.390
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: you go to jail.

asr-000730
00:49:39.400 --> 00:49:40.950
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Our Constitution

asr-000731
00:49:40.960 --> 00:49:43.497
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: mentions about final judgment.

asr-000732
00:49:43.960 --> 00:49:45.623
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, we have the right to appeal

asr-000733
00:49:45.960 --> 00:49:48.309
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: and the worst criminal

asr-000734
00:49:48.319 --> 00:49:49.555
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: who has been convicted

asr-000735
00:49:50.119 --> 00:49:57.858
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: has the, has the, has the, has the, uh, uh, has he, has she, has

asr-000736
00:49:58.280 --> 00:50:00.589
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: the, the opportunity to always question

asr-000737
00:50:00.599 --> 00:50:02.589
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Because of the presumption

asr-000738
00:50:02.599 --> 00:50:04.430
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: of innocence.

asr-000739
00:50:04.440 --> 00:50:07.589
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, we ask our dear Ombudsman

asr-000740
00:50:07.599 --> 00:50:08.670
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: to comment on that.

asr-000741
00:50:08.680 --> 00:50:10.190
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Because the proposal

asr-000742
00:50:10.200 --> 00:50:12.750
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: for them to go directly to jail

asr-000743
00:50:12.760 --> 00:50:14.390
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: precisely contradicts

asr-000744
00:50:14.400 --> 00:50:16.470
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: the constitutional presumption

asr-000745
00:50:16.480 --> 00:50:17.770
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: of innocence.

asr-000746
00:50:18.240 --> 00:50:19.643
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Your Honor,

asr-000747
00:50:20.280 --> 00:50:22.109
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: it is a presumption of innocence

asr-000748
00:50:22.119 --> 00:50:22.910
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: is very important.

asr-000749
00:50:22.920 --> 00:50:24.065
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I agree with you.

asr-000750
00:50:24.720 --> 00:50:27.322
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But when a person is convicted,

asr-000751
00:50:27.920 --> 00:50:29.510
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: we have already armed

asr-000752
00:50:29.520 --> 00:50:31.710
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: the court has already given its judgment

asr-000753
00:50:31.720 --> 00:50:34.342
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: as to the guilt or innocence of the accused.

asr-000754
00:50:34.960 --> 00:50:36.750
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It's not even a disputable presumption.

asr-000755
00:50:36.760 --> 00:50:38.527
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It's something that has to be put

asr-000756
00:50:38.920 --> 00:50:39.961
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: into the hands of the court.

asr-000757
00:50:40.799 --> 00:50:43.670
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But that presumption disappears.

asr-000758
00:50:43.680 --> 00:50:46.643
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: The presumption of innocence disappears

asr-000759
00:50:47.319 --> 00:50:47.858
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: once a court

asr-000760
00:50:49.359 --> 00:50:50.153
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: armed with jurisdiction

asr-000761
00:50:51.000 --> 00:50:52.246
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: sentences a person

asr-000762
00:50:52.680 --> 00:50:53.258
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: to jail.

asr-000763
00:50:54.040 --> 00:50:55.250
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: That's what I believe, Your Honor.

asr-000764
00:50:55.599 --> 00:50:57.150
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It becomes...

asr-000765
00:50:57.160 --> 00:50:59.150
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It's not even a disputable

asr-000766
00:50:59.160 --> 00:50:59.990
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: presumption.

asr-000767
00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:01.549
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: The presumption of innocence

asr-000768
00:51:01.559 --> 00:51:02.950
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: is already overturned

asr-000769
00:51:02.960 --> 00:51:04.227
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: by a conviction, Your Honor.

asr-000770
00:51:05.559 --> 00:51:07.349
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: We have a difference of opinion

asr-000771
00:51:07.760 --> 00:51:08.210
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: that, yes,

asr-000772
00:51:09.839 --> 00:51:10.403
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Congressman, please proceed.

asr-000773
00:51:11.400 --> 00:51:12.817
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: Thank you. Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-000774
00:51:13.559 --> 00:51:15.470
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: My question really was not

asr-000775
00:51:15.480 --> 00:51:16.910
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: directed at the issue of bail,

asr-000776
00:51:16.920 --> 00:51:18.829
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: although I do agree that

asr-000777
00:51:18.839 --> 00:51:20.829
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: the Supreme Court should revisit

asr-000778
00:51:20.839 --> 00:51:23.270
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: issues about bail pending appeal.

asr-000779
00:51:23.280 --> 00:51:25.670
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: Ang tanong ko po ay ganito.

asr-000780
00:51:25.680 --> 00:51:27.270
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: Assuming meron nang na-convict

asr-000781
00:51:27.280 --> 00:51:28.390
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: ng Sandigan Bayan,

asr-000782
00:51:28.400 --> 00:51:29.150
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: pinrosecute,

asr-000783
00:51:29.160 --> 00:51:30.710
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: ng ombudsman.

asr-000784
00:51:30.720 --> 00:51:33.109
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: You spend millions of pesos

asr-000785
00:51:33.119 --> 00:51:35.497
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: taking that prosecution to conviction.

asr-000786
00:51:36.000 --> 00:51:37.910
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: The accused now

asr-000787
00:51:37.920 --> 00:51:38.838
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: makes an appeal.

asr-000788
00:51:39.280 --> 00:51:41.230
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: The appeal can last anywhere

asr-000789
00:51:41.240 --> 00:51:42.910
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: from a few years to

asr-000790
00:51:42.920 --> 00:51:44.270
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: many, many years.

asr-000791
00:51:44.280 --> 00:51:47.789
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: Pag bumaba yung appeal, na-affirm ang conviction,

asr-000792
00:51:47.799 --> 00:51:49.150
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: many things can happen

asr-000793
00:51:49.160 --> 00:51:50.990
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: before that person is actually

asr-000794
00:51:51.000 --> 00:51:52.789
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: apprehended and put to jail

asr-000795
00:51:52.799 --> 00:51:54.430
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: to serve his sentence.

asr-000796
00:51:54.440 --> 00:51:56.829
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: Ang tanong ko po ay, apparently,

asr-000797
00:51:56.839 --> 00:51:58.950
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: there is no centralized system

asr-000798
00:51:58.960 --> 00:52:01.282
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: that our government has to track that

asr-000799
00:52:02.040 --> 00:52:03.829
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: so that maraming nakakalusot

asr-000800
00:52:03.839 --> 00:52:06.230
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: na sayang lang ang ginawa natin

asr-000801
00:52:06.240 --> 00:52:08.150
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: pag-prosecute na convict,

asr-000802
00:52:08.160 --> 00:52:09.829
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: hindi naman pala nakulong.

asr-000803
00:52:09.839 --> 00:52:11.670
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: Now, does that bother

asr-000804
00:52:11.680 --> 00:52:13.109
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: the office of the ombudsman?

asr-000805
00:52:13.119 --> 00:52:15.069
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: Have you undertaken any efforts

asr-000806
00:52:15.079 --> 00:52:16.910
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: to create that system?

asr-000807
00:52:16.920 --> 00:52:20.030
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: Because this has to go beyond your office.

asr-000808
00:52:20.040 --> 00:52:22.030
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: Kailangan po magkakasama po diyan

asr-000809
00:52:22.040 --> 00:52:24.349
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: ang Department of Justice,

asr-000810
00:52:24.359 --> 00:52:25.630
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: ang BuCor,

asr-000811
00:52:25.640 --> 00:52:27.109
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: and other agencies so that

asr-000812
00:52:27.119 --> 00:52:29.024
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: we have that system to track.

asr-000813
00:52:29.440 --> 00:52:30.869
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: May I have your views on that,

asr-000814
00:52:30.879 --> 00:52:31.775
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: Ombudsman Remulla?

asr-000815
00:52:32.240 --> 00:52:34.150
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I agree wholeheartedly, Your Honor,

asr-000816
00:52:34.160 --> 00:52:36.710
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: that we need to track all of these convictions.

asr-000817
00:52:36.720 --> 00:52:39.048
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: In fact, in our budget presentation,

asr-000818
00:52:39.440 --> 00:52:41.390
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: we asked for funding

asr-000819
00:52:41.400 --> 00:52:42.549
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: for the creation of the office

asr-000820
00:52:42.559 --> 00:52:44.093
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: of the Ombudsman Marshal,

asr-000821
00:52:44.559 --> 00:52:46.186
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: which will be given that

asr-000822
00:52:46.760 --> 00:52:48.110
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: responsibility to track

asr-000823
00:52:48.480 --> 00:52:50.641
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: the status of all the persons

asr-000824
00:52:51.799 --> 00:52:52.829
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: in jail

asr-000825
00:52:52.839 --> 00:52:55.349
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: or sentenced to jail

asr-000826
00:52:55.359 --> 00:52:56.510
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: or accused

asr-000827
00:52:56.520 --> 00:52:58.572
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: so that we will have a complete

asr-000828
00:53:02.920 --> 00:53:03.950
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: inventory of the people

asr-000829
00:53:03.960 --> 00:53:05.549
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: who are being charged in the court,

asr-000830
00:53:05.559 --> 00:53:06.942
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: in our legal system, Your Honor.

asr-000831
00:53:07.760 --> 00:53:09.254
Rep. Jose Manuel Tadeo "Chel" I. Diokno: Thank you, Ombudsman.

asr-000832
